  "localContent": "Bottom of the existing porch railing against the street. The thick left-center upright descends from beyond the top to its ground contact around mid-height; a second narrow upright at the right continues lower. Existing diagonal rails and chunky timber infill occupy the upper-right only. The lower half and left edge are natural pale grey stone ground, including only the few existing red paper scrap patches near the lower-left. Preserve the actual wood-to-stone silhouettes and the attached shadows at the post feet. Do not add furniture, extra posts, a raised planter, new railing caps, or additional festive objects.\nThis crop has NO blue/blue-grey inset border, NO ribbon, NO narrow diagonal contrasting paving strip. Any general instruction about road borders is CONDITIONAL and does not apply here. Continue only the ordinary large grey paving slabs from the left native anchor and their existing thin grout lines across the floor. Do not add ornamental column pedestals or carved cloud blocks: the wooden railing posts terminate simply on the grey paving at the guide positions, with small restrained foot shadows. Preserve existing red paper scraps shown near lower left and preserve the exact wooden railing geometry from the top native anchor. Do not turn any x115/y230 anchor boundary into an object edge.",
